# LeakSanitizer suppressions for Obvious Edit — library one-time
# initialization ONLY (companion to tests/valgrind.supp; see its scope
# policy). The ASan/UBSan battery runs the same suites as the Valgrind
# gate, so the same upstream-owned caches need the same scoped relief
# here: LSan's reachability analysis cannot see fontconfig's
# process-global config pointers and reports its one-time
# FcInitLoadConfigAndFonts() caches (config XML, font index, the
# resolved pattern cairo_toy_font_face_create keeps alive) as leaks.
# No project-code allocation may ever be listed here.
#
# Observed on libfontconfig 2.15.0 / libcairo 1.18.4 (Debian 13):
# 512 bytes definite + 172 bytes indirect, zero project-code frames.
leak:libfontconfig.so
